29,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Minato,,"It's sad, but the coordination group is understaffed and our developers are busy until the third quarter. We can't ask them for more.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I found that network coverage at customer plants is very unreliable, and some visitor approvals take weeks. Also, tools requiring daily entry from everyone usually fail.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,George,,"The capital budget is frozen, though we have some software allowance. Interestingly, fixed-fee work is stable, but per-head licences will get more expensive as we grow.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,May,,"Jonathan is right about the rollouts. Also, most cross-unit standardization efforts failed because they had no owner, except for the tool room walkthroughs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Midori,,"People are losing an hour every day just copying records. Also, we have misrouted deliveries because different units have different addresses for the same firms.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@George, if the budget is frozen, does that mean we can only do things that use the software allowance?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, the copying and delivery issues sound like they could be solved by a central system, but we must avoid anything that requires constant daily data entry.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,George,,"@Minato, essentially yes. We must be very careful about recurring costs, especially if they scale with the number of users.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, the fact that ""narrow tools"" survive while broad ones fail is a huge warning. We shouldn't pick something that tries to force everyone to change their habits.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I agree. But the waste of time is real. If we can fix the address and copying issues without adding a huge burden, it would help everyone.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, if the network is bad at plants, maybe we shouldn't pick something that needs a constant internet connection?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, that is a very sharp observation. Any field-based tool would be a gamble given the signal drops and the approval delays.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,George,,I am concerned that any project requiring a large-scale rollout of licences will eventually break our budget in the renewal year.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,May,,"It seems we need something narrow, low-maintenance, and not dependent on external site access or a massive amount of new developer time.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I just want something that stops the frustration of the staff. If we can consolidate the records, the daily stress would go down.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
