54,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,1,talk,Minato,,"The candidates are Workflow Assistant, Training Studio, Supplier Data Hub, and Field Service App. I think the Workflow Assistant sounds like it might be too much extra work.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I must object to the Field Service App. With the network issues and visitor approvals I found, it is far too risky to deploy.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,George,,"The Supplier Data Hub sounds like it could involve many licences. The Training Studio might be a fixed-fee production, which is safer for the budget.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,May,,"The Supplier Data Hub is a ""standardization effort,"" and those usually fail without an owner. The Workflow Assistant requires daily entry, which also fails.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Midori,,The Supplier Data Hub would solve the misrouted deliveries and the copying of records. It addresses the actual problems the staff are facing.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Midori, but who will update the Hub? If the coordination group is already empty, will it just be more work for the same tired people?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, that's a fair point. The Training Studio is a set of modules; once they are built, they don't require daily maintenance from the staff.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,George,,"@Midori, if the Hub uses per-head licences for every unit, it will be a financial burden. The Training Studio is a one-time production cost.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,May,,"@George, I agree. The Training Studio is a ""narrow tool"" for skill transfer, similar to the tool room walkthroughs that actually worked.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, but the Training Studio doesn't stop the delivery errors or the copying. The Hub is more useful, even if it's harder to start.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Minato,,I feel the Training Studio is the kindest choice. It helps people learn without adding a new daily chore to their list.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. It avoids the network risks of the App and the ""daily entry"" failure pattern of the Assistant and the Hub.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,George,,"From a budget perspective, the Training Studio is the most predictable. No scaling licences, no frozen capital issues.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,May,,"It's the only one that fits the pattern of success. It's a resource, not a process. I vote for the Training Studio.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I still wish we could fix the data issues, but I don't want to pick something that will be dropped after a year. I'll go with the Studio.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Minato,,I vote for the Training Studio.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for the Training Studio.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,George,,I vote for the Training Studio.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,May,,I vote for the Training Studio.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Midori,,I vote for the Training Studio.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
